  "description": "Erection of one 2 storey x 4 bed detached house with parking, cycle storage, PV Panels, landscaping and all amenities following demolition of existing garage",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed dwelling would, by reason of its height, bulk and close proximity to the southern boundary of the site be intrusive, overbearing and unneighbourly in relation to no. 203a Wennington Road and well as giving rise to material overlooking and loss of privacy to occupiers of both 203 and 203a Wennington Road, thereby having a significant adverse effect on the amenities of these adjacent occupiers contrary to Policy 7 of the Havering Local Plan and the Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document.",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its scale and design, in particular its excessive width and footprint gives rise to a poor quality development, which is cramped within the plot and at odds with the general appearance and arrangement of dwellings within the Ingrebourne Road streetscene.  Furthermore, it results in a poor quality living environment for future occupiers due to proximity of the ground floor main habitable room windows to the rear boundary of the site, giving rise to poor outlook from the main rear ground floor habitable room windows. The design approach adopted would result in substandard residential accommodation to the detriment of the amenity of future occupants of this proposed 4-bed dwelling.  The proposals would therefore be contrary to Policies 10, 7 and 26 of the Havering Local Plan 2016-2031 and Policy D6 of the London Plan.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, it was necessary to issue a decision as close to the statutory timeframe as possible as opposed to seeking amendments which would have significantly delayed the application.",
    "In the event that this application is allowed through the appeals process the proposals would be liable for the following CIL contributions:",
    "Mayoral CIL (MCIL2) contribution of £4037.50 (x £25 per sqm).",
    "Havering CIL (HCIL) contribution of £20,187.50 (x £125 per sqm).",
    "Each contribution would be subject to indexation."
  ],
